{
  "category": "Rushing Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "LINOONE always runs full speed and only in straight lines. If facing an obstacle, it makes a right-angle turn to evade it. This POKéMON is very challenged by gently curving roads.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "When hunting, LINOONE will make a beeline straight for the prey at a full run. While this POKéMON is capable of topping 60 mph, it has to come to a screeching halt before it can turn.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is exceedingly fast if it only has to run in a straight line. When it spots pond- dwelling prey underwater, it quickly leaps in and catches it with its sharp claws.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "When running in a straight line, it can top 60 miles per hour. However, it has a tough time with curved roads.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "When running in a straight line, it can top 60 miles per hour. However, it has a tough time with curved roads.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It charges prey at speeds over 60 mph. However, because it can only run straight, it often fails.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It charges prey at speeds over 60 mph. However, because it can only run straight, it often fails.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
